<title>POLAND: Polish trade gap grows to $6.43 bln in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Polish trade gap grows to $6.43 bln in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's registered trade gap in the first five months of 1997 amounted to $6.43 billion, against $4.37 billion in the same period of last year, the Central Statistical Office said (GUS).  </p>
<p> POLISH TRADE (MLN USD)     JAN-MAY 97	   JAN-MAY 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		    -6,435		  -4,36</p>
<p> exports			    10,162		     N.A.</p>
<p> imports			    16,597		     N.A.</p>
<p> TRADE WITH EU		  JAN-MAY 97	   JAN-MAY 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		    -3,902		     N.A.</p>
<p> exports			     6,689		     N.A.</p>
<p> imports			    10,592		     N.A.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
